From: soundgoof <soundgoof@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 00:51:06 +0200
Subject: fix: initialize alpns in httptest.c SSL options to avoid uninitialized read

add_http_test() allocates a per-request ssloptions_t with malloc() when a
URL specifies a custom cipher list, SSL version, or client certificate, but
never sets the alpns field added by 75cfe50b (ALPN support). setup_ssl() in
contest.c later checks item->ssloptions->alpns as a fallback and calls
strdup() on it, so uninitialized heap memory can be read as a string pointer.

Origin: upstream, commit:f090908334384d6e1851f8f32af652e2e466494a
---
 xymonnet/httptest.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xymonnet/httptest.c b/xymonnet/httptest.c
index 7c05b1d1..f8346450 100644
--- a/xymonnet/httptest.c
+++ b/xymonnet/httptest.c
@@ -683,6 +683,7 @@ void add_http_test(testitem_t *t)
 		sslopt->cipherlist = sslopt_ciphers;
 		sslopt->sslversion = sslopt_version;
 		sslopt->clientcert = sslopt_clientcert;
+		sslopt->alpns = NULL;
 	}
 
 	/* Add to TCP test queue */
